timestamp=2026-11-04T19:15:23.939Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/tmp/candidate_stats.csv')\n# Look for low correlation even at best lag? Or large improvement at lag? (rhythm different -> timing shifted)\n# \"One problematic station broadly follows local patterns, but not with the same rhythm as its peers.\" -> maybe similar shape but shifted in time? so corr at 0 is lower, but best_corr at non-zero lag is much higher, and comparable amplitude\n# Find such cases\n# Also \"swings are unusually muted compared with comparable local stations\" -> amp_ratio small (e.g. < ~0.8) but maybe corr reasonable?\n# Also \"appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver\" -> ordinary aggregate stats, but correlation to a specific weather driver unusually high after accounting for peers? Or just very high corr to some specific weather var?\n\n# First clue: rhythm different\nrhythm = df[(df['best_corr'] - df['corr'] > 0.1) & (df['amp_ratio'].between(0.7, 1.5))].sort_values('best_corr - corr', ascending=False)\nprint('=== RHYTHM candidates (big lag improvement) ===')\nprint(rhythm.head(15).to_string())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
