timestamp=2026-11-04T19:17:36.035Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Look at the 3rd clue more precisely: \"A third appears ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver.\"\n# \"remaining deviations\" - probably after accounting for peers/local trend. We looked at residuals vs weather. \n# Is any of these \"ordinary in aggregate\" (normal corr with peers, normal amp_ratio)? \n# Compare to our earlier stats\nstats = pd.read_csv('/tmp/candidate_stats.csv')\nres = pd.read_csv('/tmp/resid_weather_corr.csv')\n\n# Join\nmerged = res.merge(stats, left_on='st', right_on='st', suffixes=('', '_st'))\nmerged = merged.sort_values('abs_corr', ascending=False)\nprint(merged.head(15)[['st','pol','dist','wvar','corr','abs_corr','corr_st','amp_ratio','best_corr']].to_string())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
