timestamp=2026-11-04T19:18:48.534Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# ST005 has moderate residual-temp correlation (|0.49|). Is that \"too neatly lined up with one environmental driver\"? \n# Compared to others, some have higher |corr| like ST040 (0.67), ST060 (0.66), ST023 (0.64). \n# Also ST039 has 0.64 with wind. These are quite high.\n# But which one fits \"appears ordinary in aggregate\"? ST005 has corr ~0.56, amp_ratio ~0.99 - very ordinary. \n# Others with high residual-weather corr: ST040 has amp_ratio 2.86 (not ordinary, swings very large), ST060 has corr with peers only 0.44 (not ordinary, doesn’t follow peers well), ST039 has corr ~0.73 and amp_ratio ~1.53 (amplified), ST023 has amp_ratio ~1.48 (amplified).\n# So ST005 is the only one that’s ordinary in aggregate (corr~0.56, amp~1.0) but still has the strongest residual alignment with temperature among “ordinary” stations? Or at least notable. That fits the third case.\n# That gives us: Case 1 (rhythm/lag) -> ST020, Case 2 (muted swings) -> ST051, Case 3 (ordinary aggregate but residuals too aligned with env driver) -> ST005? Let’s verify.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
