timestamp=2026-11-04T19:20:07.278Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# ST005 has 3 NaNs - small gaps. But the pattern: follows district median quite closely in timing and amplitude. Residuals correlate with temperature moderately. That fits \"ordinary in aggregate, but its remaining deviations line up a bit too neatly with one environmental driver\" (temperature as the driver). That’s plausible.\n\n# Compare Case 3 alternatives again. ST060 had very high residual-rain corr (0.66) and also many NaNs (9) and low corr with peers (0.44). It doesn’t really look “ordinary in aggregate”. So probably not ST060. ST023 had high residual-rain corr but amp_ratio 1.48 (amplified) - not ordinary. ST039: amplified swings, high corr with peers but not “ordinary in the sense of typical amplitude”? Also ST040 has extreme amp_ratio. So ST005 is the best fit for Case 3.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
