timestamp=2026-11-04T19:20:13.629Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# Let’s also confirm the other two candidates more strongly.\n# Case 1: ST020 (PM10, PSIE_POLE) - large lag improvement (corr 0.16 -> 0.59 at lag 1). That means it’s shifted in time relative to peers. “not with the same rhythm as its peers” strongly matches phase shift. Yes.\n\n# Case 2: ST051 (PM25, FABRYCZNA) - muted swings (amp_ratio 0.82, std 3.24 vs peers ~5-7), corr still ~0.63. Plausible point-by-point but muted. Yes.\n\n# Case 3: ST005 (PM10, FABRYCZNA) - ordinary aggregate (amp ~1.0, follows peers reasonably), but residuals align with temperature (|0.49|) more than most “ordinary” stations. Also within same district as ST051 (FABRYCZNA)? ST051 and ST005 are both in FABRYCZNA but different pollutants - PM25 vs PM10. That’s fine.\n\n# So the three faulty stations are likely {ST020, ST051, ST005}.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
