timestamp=2026-11-04T19:23:42.318Z level=INFO run=b8e4cffa message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\n# ST058 is in that “ordinary-ish” range for Case 3? corr_x (resid-weather corr) is 0.54, amp_ratio 0.94, but also ST058 had low corr with district median (corr_st from earlier was low) and big lag improvement - that’s Case 1 behavior too. So ST058 is ambiguous.\n# ST005 has corr with peers 0.56, amp_ratio 0.99 - very cleanly “ordinary in aggregate”. And its residual correlation to temperature is 0.49. That fits the Case 3 description best without overlapping other cases as strongly.\n# So the three are: ST020 (rhythm), ST051 (muted), ST005 (residual-env alignment, ordinary aggregate). These don’t overlap in the obvious ways and match each description.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
